liuqin: add the IOHIDDevice half the userland actually opens (touch)

`docs/HID_LAST_MILE.md` pinned the touch gap with probes: backboardd opens an
IOHIDDevice service with connect type 0x484944 (kIOHIDLibUserClientConnectManager)
and this tree has no IOHIDDevice.cpp / IOHIDLibUserClient.cpp at all -- only the
key/type headers. The IOHIDEventService path (LiuqinHID.cpp) is a dead end for
the digitizer; the userland never opens those services.

This patch vendors the device half from Apple's
apple-oss-distributions/IOHIDFamily at tag IOHIDFamily-1915.140.3 (the version
HID_LAST_MILE.md names as the closest published source to this root's 16.6.1
userland), unchanged except for the licence headers staying intact:

  IOHIDDevice.cpp                  the device object: properties, queues, reports
  IOHIDLibUserClient.cpp           the 'HID' user client the userland opened
  IOHIDElementPrivate.cpp          element tree built from the report descriptor
  IOHIDElementContainer.cpp        element storage
  IOHIDEventQueue.cpp              event queue
  IOHIDReportElementQueue.cpp      report queue
  IOHIDDeviceElementContainer.cpp  element lookup
  + the headers those need (IOHIDDevice.h, IOHIDDescriptorParserPrivate.h,
    IOHIDFamilyPrivate.h, IOHIDInterface.h, AppleHIDUsageTables.h, ...)

and wires them into iokit/conf/files.arm64.

Not yet in this patch, and needed before touch works: the macOS-only names
IOHIDDevice.cpp references (IOHIDSystemActivityTickle, IOHIKeyboard,
IOHIPointing, kIOHIDSystemDeviceSeizeRequestMessage) still need stubs, and the
digitizer still has to be published as an IOHIDDevice with a multitouch report
descriptor the userland accepts. See docs/HID_DEVICE_PORT_PLAN.md for the
remaining steps; this commit is the compile check for the vendored sources.


